WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:02.905
At staff level, depth is assumed.

2
00:00:02.925 --> 00:00:04.643
The loop scores what you do with it.

3
00:00:04.663 --> 00:00:07.040
Most staff rejections happen here.

4
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:12.640
Four skills: frame the problem, set a direction, review a design, and influence.

5
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.115
First: senior or staff?

6
00:00:14.135 --> 00:00:15.575
Hear the difference.

7
00:00:15.595 --> 00:00:19.960
A senior answer solves the problem in front of it, and solves it well.

8
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.785
A staff answer asks: is this the right problem?

9
00:00:22.805 --> 00:00:24.910
And who else has it?

10
00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.420
Second: make our data trustworthy.

11
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.220
That ask is vague on purpose.

12
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:30.880
Do not start to build.

13
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:31.992
Find who is hurt.

14
00:00:32.012 --> 00:00:33.418
Find the real problem.

15
00:00:33.438 --> 00:00:36.155
Then commit to one first step.

16
00:00:36.175 --> 00:00:39.065
Third: choose a direction for several teams.

17
00:00:39.085 --> 00:00:42.925
A strategy says where we are, where we go, and in which order.

18
00:00:42.945 --> 00:00:45.825
In a design review, find the few flaws that matter.

19
00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:48.150
Skip the small ones.

20
00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:50.485
Last: nobody reports to you.

21
00:00:50.505 --> 00:00:54.070
So you move people with evidence, and with what they care about.

22
00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:56.008
And put a price on the decision.

23
00:00:56.028 --> 00:00:58.570
Include the time of the people.

24
00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:01.130
Quick recap of staff-level judgement.

25
00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:02.355
Question the problem.

26
00:01:02.375 --> 00:01:03.655
Commit to a first step.

27
00:01:03.675 --> 00:01:05.790
And move people with evidence.

28
00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:08.910
Now start the first lesson below.
